# apps/cron-worker never ships in the Fly image, and the builder stage never
# installs its devDependencies (wrangler, workers-types): the Dockerfile copies
# only the web/engine/reference manifests before `pnpm install`. Left in the
# context, ci.yml's container job (`turbo run typecheck` inside the image)
# would fail on it with TS2688.
apps/cron-worker
# tools/ holds the dev-only harnesses (ruling 56): tools/matrix (@seazn/matrix)
# today, the scheduler bench later. Nothing the image builds or type-checks may
# import them: scripts/__tests__/tools-import-guard.test.ts and the eslint rule
# from scripts/lib/tools-import-guard.mjs hold apps/, packages/ and scripts/ to
# that. Ignoring the directory also keeps its workspace manifest out of the
# build context, so the Dockerfile never COPYs it, exactly like
# apps/cron-worker above.
tools/
